Comments
********

.[perex]
Only two things in ordinary comments matter to the `comments` section: a single-line comment written with `#` instead of `//`, and an empty `//` left behind when its text was deleted. The [spacing |spacing#spacing.comment.marker] section sets the space after `//`, and the [phpdoc |phpdoc] section covers doc comments.

```neon
comments:
	singleline: '//'
	empty: forbidden
```

```php .[before]
# the total of the cart  // A single-line comment must start with `//`, not `#`.
$total = 0;
//
$count = 0;  // Empty comment.
```

```php .[after]
// the total of the cart
$total = 0;
$count = 0;
```

An attribute `#[...]` is not a comment, so `singleline` leaves it alone.


comments.empty
==============

An empty comment, which is removed.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `keep` · covers `no_empty_comment`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.EmptyComment` .[decision-facts]


comments.firstColumn
====================

A `//` or `#` comment on a line of its own in the first column of an indented block, as an editor comments a line out, the indentation of the line after the marker; where it may not stand there, it takes the indentation of the line below it and the marker loses the indentation it doubles.

Not a `/* */` comment.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `optional`: there or not, as the author wrote it

Default `forbidden` · standards: perCs `forbidden`, psr12 `forbidden`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` .[decision-facts]


comments.singleline
===================

The marker of a single-line comment.

- `'//'`: `//`, never `#`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `'//'`, symfony `'//'`, laravel `'//'` · covers `single_line_comment_style`, `PEAR.Commenting.InlineComment` .[decision-facts]

{{maintitle: PHP Comment Rules}}
